(Title) Tj
T*
(Effectiveness of an integrative exercise and health education program for metabolic) Tj
T*
(syndrome: protocol for a randomized comparative trial in a Latin American community) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Metabolic syndrome represents a significant public health challenge throughout Latin) Tj
T*
(America, yet evidence-based community interventions remain underutilized in clinical) Tj
T*
(practice. This protocol describes an 18-week structured program designed to improve) Tj
T*
(cardiometabolic health through supervised aerobic activity, evidence-based nutrition and) Tj
T*
(lifestyle education, and regular clinical monitoring. A single-center randomized design) Tj
T*
(will enroll approximately 80 adults with confirmed metabolic syndrome from community) Tj
T*
(health centers. Participants will be randomly allocated to either the integrated exercise-) Tj
T*
(and-education program or standard care. The intervention comprises three supervised) Tj
T*
(aerobic sessions weekly, monthly group health-education workshops, and biweekly clinical) Tj
T*
(assessments including weight and metabolic measures. Primary outcomes examine changes in) Tj
T*
(cardiorespiratory fitness, body composition measures, and metabolic markers including) Tj
T*
(lipids and glucose. Secondary assessments will measure functional capacity, self-reported) Tj
T*
(health status, and adherence rates. Data collection occurs at baseline and 18-week) Tj
T*
(completion. This pragmatic protocol outlines a scalable community model for metabolic) Tj
T*
(syndrome management in resource-limited settings.) Tj
